data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"With $\\mathbf{p}_i = \\operatorname{softmax}(\\mathbf{z}_i)$ and true class $t_i$, the loss is\n$L = -\\frac1n\\sum_i\\big(z_{i,t_i} - \\operatorname{logsumexp}(\\mathbf{z}_i)\\big)$. The gradient is\n$\\partial L/\\partial\\mathbf{z}_i = (\\mathbf{p}_i - \\mathbf{e}_{t_i})/n$. Compute the log-sum-exp with the row maximum\nsubtracted, and take the true-class term from the logits, not from the probability."},"hints_note":null}

