data: {"level":3,"reviewed":{"level":3,"label":"code shape","text":"Validate: `logits` is a non-empty 2-D array with `k >= 2` and finite entries; `targets` is 1-D with length `n`,\nhas an integer dtype (check `np.issubdtype(dtype, np.integer)`), and lies in `[0, k)`. Then compute\n`shifted = z - z.max(axis=1, keepdims=True)`, the row sums of `exp(shifted)`, the log-probabilities, the loss\nat `rows, targets`, and adjust probabilities at the true-class positions for the gradient. Divide by `n` before summing large row losses. An overflowing true-class gap can still have a representable batch contribution: scale its original terms before subtracting."},"hints_note":null}

